module fluorescence

manifest cell_suspension
manifest bead_detection_reagent

instructions:

// Step 1: Co-encapsulate the cell suspension (antibody-secreting 9E10 hybridoma cells mixed
// with non-secreting K562 cells) with the bead/detection-antibody reagent (streptavidin beads
// coated with anti-mouse-Fc capture antibody, plus a DyLight 488-labeled anti-mouse-Fab
// detection antibody) into a single 50-pl droplet
cells = dispense cell_suspension
beads = dispense bead_detection_reagent
droplet = mix cells with beads

// Step 2: Keep droplets cold (~4 C) during handling to slow cellular metabolism, then shift
// to 37 C for 15 min to induce antibody secretion; secreted antibody is captured on the bead
// and recruits the fluorescent detection probe, concentrating fluorescence on the bead
heat droplet at 4c for 60s
heat droplet at 37c for 900s

// Step 3: Fluorescence-activated droplet analysis -- measure green fluorescence intensity
// (bead-localized DyLight 488 signal from captured secreted antibody)
green_signal = detect fluorescence on droplet for 5s

// Step 4: Droplet sorting -- droplets with fluorescence above the sorting threshold
// (~1.5 RFU, ~3x the ~0.5 RFU background/detection threshold) are diverted by
// dielectrophoresis into the collection channel; droplets below threshold flow by default
// into the waste channel
if (green_signal < 1.5) {
    dispose droplet
}
